t; later bytes are never parsed, even if malformed. Failures: a stream that closes without a terminal event throws `StreamIncompleteError`; a final frame that never received its blank line is discarded (as the SSE specification says) and so also counts as incomplete. Invalid JSON, a payload that is not an object with a string `type`, or a known event type with an invalid shape throws `StreamProtocolError` (the message names the event and field and never echoes the payload). A failed read throws `StreamInterruptedError` with the original error as `cause`; an `AbortError` is rethrown unchanged. All three extend `AskStreamError`. Unknown event types: `parseStreamEvent` returns `null` and the stream reader skips them, so an old client survives a new server event type. A stream consisting only of unknown events is still incomplete. Framing handled: events split across chunks, several events in one chunk, CRLF (including a CR and LF in different chunks), multi-byte characters split across chunks (`TextDecoder` with `stream: true`), comment lines and frames, extra blank lines, non-data fields (`event:`, `id:`, `retry:`, ignored) and multiple `data:` lines in one frame (joined with a newline). A lone CR as a line ending is not supported. The errors live in `errors.ts`, not `parse.ts`, to avoid a circular import with `events.ts`. Tests: `tests/unit/ask-stream-events.test.ts` and `tests/unit/ask-stream-parse.test.ts` cover the four BUILD_PLAN acceptance cases plus the edge cases above and a check that no module in the folder imports `server-only`. Verified locally (as reported by the project owner): the full Vitest suite passes, including both new test files;yarn lint and yarn typecheck are clean. Not decided or tested: `maxDuration` and the `/api/ask` route (Task 1.9), the UI and its error states (Task 1.10), behaviour against a real LLM stream or a real Vercel deployment, other browsers, and any limit on how large an unfinished frame may grow in memory (the parser does not 